§ `ss 12, 13 and 14`

#ASSERT `what follows` `a bachelor` `is removed from the service` EQUALS `all contributions refunded with interest`
#ASSERT `what follows` `a bachelor` `dies in service` EQUALS `all contributions refunded with interest`
#ASSERT `what follows` `a widower without pensionable children` `retires before earning a pension` EQUALS `contributions since the last wife or child ceased refunded with interest`
#ASSERT `what follows` `married` `retires before earning a pension` EQUALS `he may go on contributing`
#ASSERT `what follows` `married` `is removed from the service` EQUALS `pension for widow or children on rights already acquired`
#ASSERT `what follows` `a widower with pensionable children` `dies in service` EQUALS `pension for widow or children under ss 30 to 38`

#ASSERT `compounded at 2.5%` 1000 0 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `compounded at 2.5%` 1000 2 EQUALS 1050.625

#ASSERT `the bachelor's refund` 1000 2 50 TRUE EQUALS 1000.625
#ASSERT `the bachelor's refund` 1000 2 50 FALSE EQUALS 1050.625

